<%#
  ============================================================================
  DESIGN MOCKUP ONLY — hardcoded, not wired up. Handing this to the
  implementation agent to bind to real state. Notes:

  1. State shown here is "on" (coursecode_enabled? == true, coursecode present).
     For the "off" state, swap the trigger pill's classes from
     `bg-success-container text-success` to `bg-surface-variant text-on-surface-variant`
     and its label from "Turned on" to "Turned off"; the row 2 code value becomes
     "—" (or course.coursecode.presence || "—").

  2. The dropdown replaces BOTH the old toggle switch and the old separate
     Generate/Re-Generate button with one control, three items:
       "Turned on"  -> enable joining (old checkbox-checked path)
       "Turned off" -> disable joining (old checkbox-unchecked path)
       "Reset"      -> regenerate the code (old link to
                       update_coursecode_course_path(course, generate: true),
                       data-turbo-method: :post)
     Reset must only be interactive when coursecode_enabled? is true — when
     off, render it inert (drop data-action / data-turbo-method, swap its
     classes to `text-on-surface-disabled cursor-not-allowed`, no hover).
     coursecode-form-handler_controller.js needs a `reset` action added
     alongside the existing toggle logic; open/close state for the menu
     itself can reuse whatever pattern the grouping-settings controller
     already uses elsewhere on this page.

  3. Reuses the app's own status-pill language (success-container / neutral
     surface-variant, per style guide §4) for the trigger, rather than
     copying Classroom's literal blue text — keeps it consistent with the
     "Approved / Pending / Redo / Neutral" pills already in this codebase.
     The chevron icon (arrow_drop_down) matches the one already used on the
     Approve split-button in the style guide.

  4. Top-level node stays exactly <turbo-frame id="course_code_form"> — do
     not add a wrapper div outside it (Turbo Stream replace() re-nests it
     otherwise — ADR-0010). The old bg-white/shadow/border/rounded-lg box is
     dropped entirely: this now sits directly inside the already-boxed
     "General" section, so it no longer needs its own card chrome.

  5. coursecode / coursecode_enabled remain outside handle_settings'
     whitelist — unchanged, this is cosmetic only.
  ============================================================================
%>
<%= turbo_frame_tag "course_code_form" do %>
  <div data-controller="coursecode-form-handler"
       data-coursecode-form-handler-url-value="<%= update_coursecode_course_path(course) %>">

    <!-- Row 1: enable/disable + reset, as one dropdown -->
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between py-2">
      <span class="text-sm font-medium text-on-surface">Allow joining via course code</span>

      <div class="relative" data-coursecode-form-handler-target="menuWrapper">
        <button type="button"
                class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 pl-3 pr-2 py-1 rounded-full text-[12px] font-medium tracking-wide bg-success-container text-success hover:bg-success-container/80 transition-colors cursor-pointer"
                data-action="click->coursecode-form-handler#toggleMenu"
                aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false">
          Turned on
          <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[16px]">arrow_drop_down</span>
        </button>

        <!-- Rendered open here for review only; agent wires visibility to the controller -->
        <div class="absolute right-0 mt-1 w-40 bg-surface border border-outline-variant rounded-[8px] shadow-soft py-1 z-10"
             data-coursecode-form-handler-target="menu">
          <button type="button"
                  class="w-full flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 text-[13px] text-on-surface bg-primary-container/40 cursor-pointer"
                  data-action="click->coursecode-form-handler#turnOn">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[16px] text-primary">check</span>
            Turned on
          </button>
          <button type="button"
                  class="w-full flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 text-[13px] text-on-surface-variant hover:bg-surface-hover cursor-pointer"
                  data-action="click->coursecode-form-handler#turnOff">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[16px] opacity-0">check</span>
            Turned off
          </button>
          <div class="my-1 border-t border-outline-variant"></div>
          <%# Enabled/"on" variant of Reset shown below. When coursecode_enabled?
              is false, replace this button's classes with
              "w-full flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 text-[13px] text-on-surface-disabled cursor-not-allowed"
              and drop data-turbo-method / data-action so it's inert. %>
          <button type="button"
                  class="w-full flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 text-[13px] text-on-surface hover:bg-surface-hover cursor-pointer"
                  data-turbo-method="post"
                  data-action="click->coursecode-form-handler#reset">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[16px] text-on-surface-variant">refresh</span>
            Reset
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Row 2: the code itself -->
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between py-2 border-t border-outline-variant">
      <span class="text-sm font-medium text-on-surface">Class code</span>
      <span class="font-mono text-sm text-on-surface-muted tracking-wide">4hbs47di</span>
      <%# course.coursecode.presence || "—" %>
    </div>

    <!-- Scope note -->
    <div class="mt-3 flex items-start gap-2 rounded-[8px] border border-warning-border bg-warning-container-alt px-3 py-2">
      <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[16px] text-warning-strong mt-0.5">info</span>
      <p class="text-[12px] text-warning-on-container leading-relaxed">
        Use this only for individual projects. For groups, use CSV imports — group formation in ProPro is coming in a future update.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
<% end %>
